Dynamic Module & Register Pattern – NestJS (Notes)
Dynamic Module
A dynamic module is a NestJS module created at runtime
Used when a module needs configuration
Returns a DynamicModule object

Common use cases:
Database configuration
Third-party libraries
Reusable shared modules


Register Pattern

Implemented using a static register() method
Accepts configuration options
Returns a DynamicModule
Allows different configurations in different modules


Basic Structure
static register(options): DynamicModule {
  return {
    module: ModuleName,
    providers: [],
    exports: [],
  };
}

Dynamic Module Structure:
@Module({})
export class SampleModule {
  static register(name: string): DynamicModule {
    return {
      module: SampleModule,
      providers: [
        { provide: 'NAME', useValue: name }
      ],
      exports: ['NAME'],
    };
  }
}
Importing Module
SampleModule.register('NestJS')
Injecting Value
constructor(@Inject('NAME') private name: string) {}


Key Points
register() → synchronous configuration
Providers can be created dynamically
Must export providers to use outside module
Enhances reusability & flexibility


One-Line Definition
Dynamic modules in NestJS allow runtime configuration using the register pattern by returning a DynamicModule